# CropperCanvas

`CropperCanvas` renders two hidden `<canvas>` elements and exports a `draw()` function that paints the cropped area of an image onto them. It is what powers the cropper's `getCanvas()` method. The second canvas is scratch space for applying rotation and flips before the crop is drawn.

The croppers render it inside the boundary, next to the background wrapper, when their `canvas` prop is `true` (the default):

```
StretchableBoundary
├─ CropperBackgroundWrapper
└─ CropperCanvas   (when canvas is true)
```

## Usage

With `Cropper` or `FixedCropper` you never touch it: call `getCanvas()` on the cropper. You need it when you build your own cropper with [`useAbstractCropper`](/docs/hooks/useAbstractCropper), which expects you to bind it into `refs.canvas`:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import {
		CropperBackgroundImage,
		CropperCanvas,
		StretchableBoundary,
		useAbstractCropper
	} from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	let { src }: { src: string } = $props();

	const { cropper, refs } = useAbstractCropper(() => ({ src }));
</script>

<StretchableBoundary bind:this={refs.boundary}>
	<CropperBackgroundImage bind:ref={refs.image} {cropper} />
	<CropperCanvas bind:this={refs.canvas} />
</StretchableBoundary>
```

`cropper.getCanvas()` then works as usual.

## Props

None.

## Exports

| Export | Signature                                                                                          | Description                                                                                                                                       |
| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `draw` | <code>(state: CropperState, image: HTMLElement, options?: DrawOptions) =&gt; HTMLCanvasElement &#124; null</code> | Draws the area `state.coordinates` of `image` (an `<img>` or a `<canvas>`), with the state's rotation and flips, and returns the result canvas. Returns `null` before the canvases exist. |

`DrawOptions` sets the size of the result and how it is drawn. The fields are described under [`getCanvas()`](/docs/components/Cropper#getcanvasoptions). The `CropperCanvasMethods` type describes the export.

The same canvas element is returned on every call and redrawn each time. To keep a result, copy it or convert it (with `toBlob()` or `toDataURL()`) before the next draw.

## CSS classes

| Element    | Classes                                       |
| ---------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Each canvas | `advanced-cropper-canvas` (hidden with `display: none`) |
